# Desktop shell rules (PRD §10, §18.3)

## Electron security (HARD RULE)
- `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`, `sandbox: true`.
- Renderer ↔ main communication ONLY through a minimal, typed, allow-listed **preload bridge**. No `remote` module, no exposing `ipcRenderer` wholesale, no Node APIs in the renderer.
- Validate every IPC payload (schema) on the main side. Treat the renderer as untrusted input.
- Restrict `webContents` navigation and `window.open`; no loading remote/untrusted content into a privileged context.

## Python sidecar lifecycle
- Main process spawns, health-checks, and gracefully shuts down the Python sidecar (`FRAMEPILOT_PYTHON_API_URL`).
- Restart/backoff on crash; surface clear status to the UI. Never leak orphaned processes on quit.
- The sidecar is the render/AI-tool engine — keep the IPC contract typed and stable.

## Atomic project save (PRD §18.3)
- `project.fp.json` saves are **atomic**: write to a temp file, fsync, then rename. Never partially overwrite the live project file.
- Keep timeline history for undo/redo.

## Crash recovery
- On startup after an unclean exit, recover from the **last valid project state** (autosave/journal). Background jobs are resumable/retryable.

## Path & secrets
- All file access goes through the safe-path sandbox (project dir). Secrets stay in `.env`; never bundle keys into the app.
